id:TASK-260720-12r55p
title:Consume shared schema v6 vectors
status:backlog
description:Extend the Python conformance harness as an independent consumer of the protocol 1.0.0-rc.5 schema, build-driver, portable execution-policy, identity, cache, context, and manager-lifecycle vectors.
scope:Own tests/test_protocol_conformance.py plus focused vector adapters and fixtures that do not duplicate product logic. Consume the exact rc.5 candidate suite through the caller-supplied CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT, whose manifest.json must hash to sha256:b6f56aacc0e37dcc6692f73f641bff761e89b645adfe20a47a06d81c6fda204c and whose release/1.0.0-rc.5.json records the same required_manifest_sha256; do not edit the committed curator-spec checkout ref in this task. Read every vector and expected artifact from that root; never hard-code a vector input the way Curator internal/godriver/controls_test.go does. Cover generated schema cases for both manifest names, agent-skill-v6 and csk-skill-v6, receipt build-receipt-v1, marker install-marker-v2, conformance-claim-v3, vectors/build-drivers.json, vectors/go-host-execution-policy.json, vectors/conformance-claim-v3-qualification.json, the 11-file expected/build-driver/ tree, and vectors/manager-lifecycle.json. build-receipt-v2, install-marker-v3, schema v7 and the external-repository and registry surfaces belong to the go-repository-v1 line and are out of scope here. The official manager suite pin remains on the previous released protocol until TASK-260720-25d05o qualifies the release and TASK-260720-1utsx8 audits the promotion. Do not import or copy Curator implementation code and do not fabricate release or conformance claims. Retained fail-closed prerequisite: the hard blockedBy edge to TASK-260720-3ag6pi is deliberately kept. TASK-260720-3ag6pi is protocol-v6-conformance-verification, is still status blocked, and is still scoped to the literal rc.4 line, and no rc.5 replacement verification gate exists on the board today, so no relink target was invented. Before this task starts, the Curator-side owner must either retarget TASK-260720-3ag6pi to this rc.5 candidate root and re-review it, or create the rc.5 verification gate and relink this edge to it; resolving that gate is Curator-side work outside this task.
ac:The Python implementation passes the shared rc.5 positive vectors for schema 6, build-root context exclusion, build-source and toolchain bytes, CCJ-1 input and key, canonical receipt and marker, fixed environment and all five Go argv forms, hit and dry-run plans, ordering, commit, rollback, recovery, status, repair, and GC, including all 8 build-drivers.json positive_cases and the byte-exact 11 artifacts under expected/build-driver/ whose cache-key.txt is sha256:529370122ae11e2e961d5265b1a020e046bcd43165b2eb96b05e73a51187ac9b and receipt-sha256.txt is sha256:919fbbad8e6ce95532219fd952c2309d0d7026f85209650508fd6834af4020cd. Named negative coverage includes every minimum cluster from the accepted rc.5 contract: all 77 build-drivers.json rejection_cases, the 10 build_source_cases and 12 toolchain_cases, and from go-host-execution-policy.json the 18 mandatory_controls, the 14 identity_and_protocol_cases, the 8 package_influence_cases, the 11 capability_evidence_cases, the 6 deferred_capability_rejection_guards, and the three failure_boundary outcomes. Execution-policy identity coverage asserts aliases false and three distinct non-alias keys: portable manager-worker-v1 valid, legacy_rc4_without_execution_policy sha256:3fcd714a40e8918eb67dbd35d435875dcce6c9047da811a1fa26626e5e57be48 invalid, and reserved_hardened sha256:13736230d33ce59de7f7323dcd4cffd510655ad8dabd5ee9e8b6cb182ec70037 invalid. Native-control inventory coverage asserts rc5-native-control-inventory-v1 is exhaustive over exactly macos and windows with exactly five controls and the declared per-platform availability and mechanism or reason. Claim coverage asserts claim-version separation across conformance-claim-v1, v2 and v3, that conformance-claim-v3 pins protocol_version 1.0.0-rc.5 and requires build_drivers, and that conformance-claim-v3-qualification.json rules hold: schema-valid-is-not-qualified, driver-platform-subset, no-generic-driver over exactly go-repository-v1 and go-v1, no-unevidenced-platform, linux excluded until TASK-260728-1skseh, and macos and windows pending-downstream-native-evidence. No conformance claim is emitted by this task. Legacy rc.3 vectors remain green. Tests against the exact caller-supplied candidate suite and strict mypy pass, the candidate revision and full manifest digest are recorded as non-release evidence, and no committed curator-spec pin or release claim changes.
blockedBy:["TASK-260720-th0jdi","TASK-260720-3ag6pi","TASK-260729-3nx97g"]
