### 7.1 Correction 1 — the stale receipt-hash claim was false

The previous §5 row claimed `750f5f75…` was "removed from the board entirely". The reviewer disproved this. The corrected §5 row now states only what is verified: the value is absent from the current `description`, `scope` and `ac` of the seven retargeted briefs (substring scan over all 21 fields, 0 hits), while 29 historical board records still carry it and are intentionally preserved. Historical evidence of the real rc.4 identity is not something this task should erase, and none of it was erased.

### 7.2 Correction 2 — `TASK-260720-12r55p.notes` restored byte-for-byte

Cycle 1 appended a 1211-character rc.5 paragraph to `TASK-260720-12r55p.notes`. `notes` is outside this task's authorized scope, which covers `description`, `scope`, `ac` and dependency edges. The append was reverted with a single `set_notes(..., set=true)` back to the exact pre-retarget content.

Pre-retarget content was reconstructed from two independent authoritative sources that agree byte-for-byte, not from reconstruction by hand:

| Source | What it is | Bytes | SHA-256 |
| --- | --- | ---: | --- |
| `STORY-260720-1uv5gi_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:11337` | the raw `set_notes` mutation result that originally wrote these notes on 2026-07-20 | 515 | `3a04adc70cd2e5499608172203a7d3ed17b4ec33e281c4c7ca7b51f24ace2500` |
| `TASK-260729-1kq1rd_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-_RUN-260728-b72cf7.log:4720` | a read-only compact board projection taken 2026-07-28, before this task ran | 515 | `3a04adc70cd2e5499608172203a7d3ed17b4ec33e281c4c7ca7b51f24ace2500` |

The live board field after restoration is 515 bytes hashing to `3a04adc70cd2e5499608172203a7d3ed17b4ec33e281c4c7ca7b51f24ace2500` — an exact match to both sources. Consistency check: the pre-restoration live value was exactly `<pre-retarget 515 bytes>` + `\n` + the 1211-character appended paragraph, confirming the cycle-1 mutation was a pure append and that nothing else in the field was disturbed.

The other six briefs were checked the same way against the 2026-07-28 pre-retarget projection: `3pemm6` (539 bytes) and `3s27te` (295 bytes) are unchanged and match, and `2dnqw2`, `2g21eg`, `akf5kh`, `th0jdi` have empty `notes` before and after. `TASK-260720-12r55p` was the only brief whose `notes` was ever mutated by this task.

### 7.3 The fail-closed gate explanation moved into `scope`

The substantive content of the reverted note is a real prerequisite and had to survive the revert, so it was rewritten into the authorized `scope` field of `TASK-260720-12r55p` (596 characters appended, 1383 → 1979). The added text states that the hard `blockedBy` edge to `TASK-260720-3ag6pi` is deliberately retained; that `3ag6pi` is still `protocol-v6-conformance-verification`, still `blocked`, and still scoped to the literal rc.4 line; that no rc.5 replacement verification gate exists on the board today so no relink target was invented; and that before `12r55p` starts, the Curator-side owner must either retarget `3ag6pi` to this rc.5 candidate root and re-review it, or create the rc.5 verification gate and relink the edge.

The `TASK-260720-jrrgw9` observation from §4.2 was deliberately **not** copied into any brief field. It is a Curator-side gate that does not govern `12r55p`'s own start condition, so putting it in a CocoaSkills brief would be scope creep. It stays in this audit.

